e":"medicare.gov, Dental services (What's covered?)","source_url":"https://www.medicare.gov/coverage/dental-services","retrieved_at":"2026-10-10T09:45:06Z","quote":"In most cases, Medicare doesn't cover dental services like routine cleanings, fillings, tooth extractions (removals), or items like dentures and implants."},{"id":"original_medicare_rule_2","source_title":"medicare.gov, Dental services (What's covered?)","source_url":"https://www.medicare.gov/coverage/dental-services","retrieved_at":"2026-10-10T09:45:06Z","quote":"Medicare may cover: Some dental services you get when you're admitted as a hospital inpatient for your dental procedure, either because of your underlying medical condition or the severity of the procedure."},{"id":"original_medicare_rule_3","source_title":"medicare.gov, Dental services (What's covered?)","source_url":"https://www.medicare.gov/coverage/dental-services","retrieved_at":"2026-10-10T09:45:06Z","quote":"Specific inpatient or outpatient dental services directly related to certain covered medical treatments."},{"id":"statute","source_title":"Social Security Act section 1862(a)(12), 42 U.S.C. 1395y(a)(12) (text as reproduced by the Legal Information Institute, Cornell Law School)","source_url":"https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/42/1395y","retrieved_at":"2026-10-10T09:45:06Z","quote":"(12) where such expenses are for services in connection with the care, treatment, filling, removal, or replacement of teeth or structures directly supporting teeth"},{"id":"regulation","source_title":"42 CFR 411.15(i) Dental services (eCFR, current)","source_url":"https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-42/section-411.15","retrieved_at":"2026-10-10T09:45:06Z","quote":"Dental services in connection with the care, treatment, filling, removal, or replacement of teeth, or structures directly supporting the teeth."},{"id":"enrollment_period","source_title":"medicare.gov, Joining a plan (enrollment periods table)","source_url":"https://www.medicare.gov/basics/g